          "quote": "For an ordinary unhooked business call, record CallStart immediately before issue. For a hook call, record it once before armHook as specified below; the same clock includes arming, acknowledgement and issue and is never restarted. A non-crashing call must emit one matching completion and permit independent readUI/readJ observations within 10000ms of CallStart on the same harness clock. Observation reads occur after completion and before another call or lifecycle control, with UI/J unchanged throughout those reads. Verify the matching instance/id, reported versus actual UI, expected complete journal, completion count observed so far and deadline. Missing, duplicate, late or mismatched results fail and cannot be erased by a later crash. ObservationComplete follows all these call-local checks within that original deadline; it permits the next call/control but is provisional. Retain every issued call id and count completions through each instance's C EOF/drain. A non-crashing invocation must have exactly one completion in that final audit; a crash-injected invocation must have zero. A late duplicate after ObservationComplete still fails. The same EOF audit requires exactly one Ready with the correct instance/J, already observed by the startup deadline; missing, wrong or duplicate Ready fails even if detected after startup confirmation. A late Ready cannot repair a startup failure. Final scenario success requires exit confirmation and the final count audit, including the final normal shutdown/exit, with no added reward call or restart during teardown.\r\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "local_id": "30",
      "statement": "Inject within-call crashes only immediately before or after the pending durable append of accept or cancel; each hook scenario must begin with its own empty J.",
      "kind": "constraint",
      "citations": [
        {
          "path": "docs/testing/story-2-5-controlled-acceptance/exclusive-resolution-v15.md",
          "raw_digest": "sha256:46453447335769fbf4d8001ade9f2090a8799809380ea0df026a0637bc67338a",
          "block_id": "SB-F7DB8CD5A9668EF4",
          "byte_start": 4244,
          "byte_end": 5519,
          "quote": "The only injected within-call crashes are immediately before or after the missing durable append of accept or cancel. Each hook scenario begins with its own empty J. Before issuing the target call, record CallStart, send armHook(i,id,op,before|after) on Q and receive its exact matching acknowledgement, where op is accept or cancel. The one-shot hook applies only to that id/op while J is empty. Before emits C:HookHit(i,id,op,before) after the empty guard and blocks before the atomic append. After emits C:HookHit(i,id,op,after) after the command's append is durable and blocks before UI finalization or Complete. No work can pass either barrier until OS termination; the harness never releases it. Observe exactly one matching acknowledgement and HookHit within the original 10000ms from CallStart, then immediately terminate i and begin its existing exit deadline. These controls are never Complete. Missing, wrong, duplicate or late hook events fail. Before leaves J empty; after leaves exactly the command's Commit or Cancel record. Confirm exit/EOF, start and confirm a new process with the unchanged J, then invoke resume under the ordinary call rule. Hooks are disabled for every other call. Failed-test cleanup cannot erase failure or count as scenario coverage.\r\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "local_id": "31",
