    },
    {
      "local_id": "55",
      "statement": "Implement the required synthetic adapter interfaces; their specification does not establish that executable endpoints already exist.",
      "kind": "obligation",
      "citations": [
        {
          "path": "docs/testing/story-2-5-controlled-acceptance/exclusive-resolution-v15.md",
          "raw_digest": "sha256:46453447335769fbf4d8001ade9f2090a8799809380ea0df026a0637bc67338a",
          "block_id": "SB-83C0467B0FFB419F",
          "byte_start": 6310,
          "byte_end": 7059,
          "quote": "These are required synthetic adapter interfaces to implement, not claims of existing executable endpoints. Protocol-design responsibility belongs to the reward-controller implementer. The downstream implementation plan must choose and document one internally consistent versioned launch/message profile, including the hook acknowledgement representation and return path, used by both controller and harness. No particular Q/C wire encoding or executable argument spelling is prescribed. Every permitted profile must preserve the event identities, command distinctions, ordering, barrier blocking, independent observations, retained completion counts, deadlines and all scenarios above. A plan leaving its selected profile unresolved is incomplete.\r\n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "local_id": "56",
      "statement": "The reward-controller implementer owns protocol design. The downstream implementation plan must choose and document one internally consistent versioned launch/message profile, including the hook acknowledgement representation and return path, for use by both controller and harness.",
